Stage: FE

Purpose:
  Frontend stage. Owns the web frontend implementation of the unit of
  work — UI, client-side state, integration against the API contract —
  everything QA needs already working before it can validate the
  feature end-to-end.


Requires:
  API (see stages/API.sdd -> Blocks)


Produces:
  Working web frontend implementation, integrated against the API
  contract, ready for QA.


Blocks:
  QA — QA MUST NOT validate a stage that has not executed (see
  chains.sdd -> Rules [C5]).


Parallel:
  MAY execute in parallel with MD when both depend only on API and are
  otherwise independent of each other (see chains.sdd ->
  ParallelExample).


Optional:
  Skipped (never silently — see chains.sdd -> Rules [C7]) when the unit
  of work has no web-frontend surface — see chains.sdd -> MobileExample,
  which shows the reverse case (MD skipped, FE required).


Skills:
  @../../skills/frontend/

  (see chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn — this file defines WHEN/responsibility
  only; HOW the frontend change is actually implemented belongs to
  skills/frontend/, not here.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/frontend/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the FE responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  that includes an FE step.
